settings.clock_howto = How to read the encoded clock
settings.clock_howto_text = The dots split the 12-hour clock face into quarters, read them from left to right:\n• 1st dot – the quarter of the clock face (3 hours): red 12–3, green 3–6, blue 6–9, brown 9–12 o'clock.\n• 2nd dot – the quarter of those 3 hours (45 min): adds 0, 45, 90 or 135 minutes (0:00, 0:45, 1:30, 2:15).\n• 3rd dot – the quarter of those 45 minutes (11¼ min): adds 0, 11, 22 or 34 minutes (exactly 11¼, 22½, 33¾).\nTime = 12:00 + 3 h × 1st + 45 min × 2nd + 11¼ min × 3rd.\nAll red = 12 o'clock (noon or midnight); the 3rd dot changes every 11¼ minutes, the 2nd every 45 minutes, the 1st every 3 hours; all brown = just before 12.\nExample: green, blue, red = 3:00 + 1:30 + 0 = 4:30 (until 4:41). Blue, red, brown = 6:00 + 0 + 0:34 ≈ 6:34.
